From: DHB_AX local port <local@invalid>
Subject: [LOCAL ONLY] net: stmmac: time the interval between receive polls

The receive ring is emptied by an occasional stall rather than by a rate
the driver cannot sustain: the backlog sits at a few dozen descriptors
whatever the ring size, and once in about thirty seconds it reaches five
hundred.  rx_desc_low_water reports that excursion but not its cause, and
three causes produce it -- the poll did not run, it ran and could not
obtain pages to hand back, or it ran and was slow.

Time the interval between consecutive receive polls and report the one
that produced the low-water reading, along with the largest interval seen.
An interval near the excursion means the poll did not run and the question
becomes what held the CPU; a short interval means it ran, and the ring
drained under it.

Separate the second cause from the third by counting the refills that end
early because the page pool has nothing to give, which is the only way a
poll that runs still returns no descriptors.

Both intervals are reset on read, alongside the low-water mark they
qualify.  An interval is offered only where the preceding poll also had
descriptors outstanding, so that the gap across idle traffic is not
reported as refill latency.
